# UST.G3CR: Selected-Source Recursive First-Jet Correction Theorem

## Statement

At the selected `GF(11)`, `gamma=3`, `a=0` proof fiber, the exact G3CQ H02
minus-divergence correction admits a complete original-Jacobian recursive
return:

```text
H02 ambient row
  -> exact H02 coordinates
  -> (1/4) divergence to H11
  -> exact H11 coordinates
  -> (1/3) divergence to H20
  -> exact H20 coordinates
  -> zero terminal divergence.
```

Every coordinate reconstruction has zero residual.  The quotient components
have respectively 229, 908, and 223 nonzero entries in H02, H11, and H20.  In
the canonical B103 order `H20(248), H11(1013), H02(248)`, they form one explicit
`1509 x 1` correction vector with 1,360 nonzero entries.

The H02 quotient agrees entrywise with the independent Singular normal form in
UST.G3CQ.  Terminality is exact because the complete H20 image domain contains
only `dPhi/du` and `dPhi/ds` multipliers independent of `u` and `s`, so its
divergence vanishes identically.

## Frontier Consequence

The selected quotient-defect branch of the family first derivative is now
closed through every Hodge block at the proof fiber.  It must not be recomputed
as an unresolved 225-generator search.

This is one contribution to the full selected connection derivative.  The
remaining work is to assemble it with any independent derivative of the
source/division data and the family variation of the lower-pole coordinate
actions, then promote that action along the G3BJ path.  Characteristic-zero
transport, integral periods and `beta_C` are not inferred here.

